---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import HeroBanner from '../components/HeroBanner.astro';
import RequirementsClusterNav from '../components/RequirementsClusterNav.astro';
import RequirementsIntakeCta from '../components/RequirementsIntakeCta.astro';

const title = 'Portugal HQA Visa Eligibility - Who Qualifies';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal HQA visa eligibility is who qualifies in 2026: the role, the host, and the applicant tests, before you assemble the supporting document checklist.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header>
      <HeroBanner
        image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility-professional.jpg"
        alt="Roman temple columns in an Évora square facing a white palace and church tower, with a carved Subscrição inscription in the foreground"
        title={title}
        items={[
          { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements', label: 'Requirements' },
          { label: 'Eligibility' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="bg-background">
        <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="max-w-3xl">
          Portugal HQA visa eligibility is the question of who may use highly qualified activity residence, before any checklist is printed. The file turns on a qualifying professional activity, a Portuguese host that can support that activity, and an applicant who can be admitted. This page does not list forms. Those belong on
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-documents" class="inline-link">HQA visa documents</a>.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>The role and the host</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Highly qualified activity is a legal test applied to the work, not a compliment on a CV. Typical hosts are a Portuguese company, university, research unit, or other entity that can contract or host the person in Portugal. A remote job for a foreign employer, with no Portuguese host, is a different analysis. A real-estate purchase does not create eligibility.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Researchers and academic hires still have to meet this role-and-host test. The
            <a href="/portugal-research-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal research visa</a>
            page covers that search phrase. It does not waive eligibility.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>The applicant</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            The person is usually a non-EU national who will carry out the activity in Portugal. Qualifications must match the role. Many employed files also have to clear a published salary floor for highly qualified activity in the year of filing. Criminal-record, identity, and subsistence rules apply in addition to the job. Confirm the 2026 floors and nationality rules with AIMA and the consulate that will see the file.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Family members are not automatic co-applicants. Whether a spouse or child can be included is a separate coverage question on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-family" class="inline-link">HQA visa family</a>
            coverage, not proof that the principal is eligible.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RequirementsIntakeCta
      source="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility"
      image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility-cta-divider.jpg"
      alt="Professional setting in Portugal used on the HQA visa eligibility page"
      heading="Find out who qualifies for the Portugal HQA visa"
      copy="Not sure whether the role, the host, and the applicant tests fit? Enter your details and our advisory team can help point you in the right direction."
    />

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>What eligibility does not cover</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Passing these tests does not assemble the pack, lodge the application, or keep the card valid. After you know the person fits, use the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa requirements</a>
            hub to move to documents. Once a card is issued, ongoing stay rules sit on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-residency-requirements" class="inline-link">HQA visa residency requirements</a>.
            For the whole route, including cost and family, return to the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
            guide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <RequirementsClusterNav current="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Test the role and the host before you collect certificates</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. Eligibility is fact-specific. A licensed professional should read the contract against the tests in force.
        </p>
        {/* TODO: no backend yet */}
        <IntakeForm source="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility" simple />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
